---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import talks from '../data/talks.json';

const recentTalks = talks.slice(0, 4);
---

<Base title="Sean Davis — Cancer Data Science">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="mark" href="/">Sean Davis</a>
      <nav>
        <a href="#work">Work</a>
        <a href="#software">Software</a>
        <a href="#writing">Writing</a>
        <a href="/talks">Talks</a>
        <a href="/blog">Notes</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="hero fade">
      <div class="place">University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus</div>
      <h1>Sean Davis</h1>
      <p class="role">Physician-scientist — open software and data for cancer research.</p>
      <p class="lede">
        For over a decade I've built open tools, curated the public biomedical record, and now build
        AI agents that help researchers find and use it. The resources I maintain are used widely across
        genomics, and core Bioconductor packages I steward bridge the field's largest data archives.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="#work">See the work</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/seandavi">GitHub</a>
        <a href="#about">About &amp; contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section id="work">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Selected work</h2>
        <div class="note">Community resources, core software, and data infrastructure.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="catalog">
        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">awesome-single-cell</h3>
            <div class="meta">3,789 stars · <span class="home">GitHub</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            The field's reference list of software and data resources for single-cell analysis — one of
            the most-starred curated resources in computational biology.
            <a class="go" href="https://github.com/seandavi/awesome-single-cell">GitHub</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">GEOquery</h3>
            <div class="meta">115 stars · <span class="home">Bioconductor</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            The bridge between the NCBI Gene Expression Omnibus and Bioconductor — a foundational R package
            I've maintained for years, used across the genomics community.
            <a class="go" href="https://seandavi.github.io/GEOquery/">Docs</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">OmicIDX</h3>
            <div class="meta"><span class="home">cancerdatasci.org</span> · open Parquet &amp; API</div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            A continuously refreshed index of the world's public sequencing metadata — SRA, GEO, and
            BioProject — served as open columnar snapshots and a query API.
            <a class="go" href="https://docs.omicidx.cancerdatasci.org">Docs</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">CFDE Atlas</h3>
            <div class="meta"><span class="home">cancerdatasci.org</span> · NIH Common Fund</div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            A knowledge base and conversational agent over the NIH Common Fund Data Ecosystem — ask across
            programs, grants, and datasets in plain language.
            <a class="go" href="https://cfde-atlas.cancerdatasci.org">Open</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">curatedMetagenomicData</h3>
            <div class="meta"><span class="home">Bioconductor</span> · uniformly processed</div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            Uniformly processed human microbiome data with curated, standardized metadata — a widely used
            resource in the Bioconductor ecosystem.
            <a class="go" href="https://cmgd.cancerdatasci.org">Open</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div>
            <h3 class="name">Orchestra</h3>
            <div class="meta"><span class="home">orchestraplatform.org</span> · training platform</div>
          </div>
          <p class="desc">
            Hosted, reproducible training environments for hands-on bioinformatics education — one-click
            workspaces the community can teach and learn in.
            <a class="go" href="https://orchestraplatform.org">Open</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="software">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>More software</h2>
        <div class="note">A selection — the full list lives on GitHub.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="group">
        <h3>AI &amp; agentic tooling</h3>
        <div class="grid">
          <a class="card" href="https://seandavi.github.io/quartobot/">
            <h4>quartobot <span class="s">5★</span></h4>
            <p>Manuscript-as-software: the manubot pattern, ergonomically, on Quarto.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://seandavi.github.io/scriptorium/">
            <h4>scriptorium <span class="s">3★</span></h4>
            <p>Coordinated AI capabilities for manuscripts, grants, and review.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/ols-mcp-server">
            <h4>ols-mcp-server <span class="s">26★</span></h4>
            <p>An MCP server for the EBI Ontology Lookup Service.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/agentic-coding-intro">
            <h4>agentic-coding-intro <span class="s">46★</span></h4>
            <p>A brief introduction to agentic coding principles and practice.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/agentic-writing-patterns">
            <h4>agentic-writing-patterns <span class="s">2★</span></h4>
            <p>Design patterns of agentic AI in scholarly writing.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/lifeos-template">
            <h4>lifeos-template <span class="s">24★</span></h4>
            <p>An opinionated, agentic life-OS for Claude Code.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="group">
        <h3>Bioconductor &amp; data tools</h3>
        <div class="grid">
          <a class="card" href="https://seandavi.github.io/BiocPkgTools/">
            <h4>BiocPkgTools <span class="s">22★</span></h4>
            <p>Build reports, package metadata, and download stats for Bioconductor.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/awesome-cancer-variant-resources">
            <h4>awesome-cancer-variant-resources <span class="s">335★</span></h4>
            <p>A community list of cancer clinical knowledge bases and databases.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/nextflow_telemetry">
            <h4>nextflow_telemetry <span class="s">5★</span></h4>
            <p>Observability and web callbacks for Nextflow workflows.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/state-cancer-profile-scraper">
            <h4>state-cancer-profile-scraper <span class="s">5★</span></h4>
            <p>Bulk access to NCI State Cancer Profiles data.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://github.com/seandavi/metacurator">
            <h4>metacurator</h4>
            <p>Spec-first, ontology-grounded reproduction of sample-level metadata.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://biomed-agents.cancerdatasci.org">
            <h4>biomedical-agent-kg <span class="s">9★</span></h4>
            <p>A knowledge graph of biomedical LLM agent systems.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="group">
        <h3>Apps</h3>
        <div class="grid">
          <a class="card" href="https://pubmed-grader.cancerdatasci.org/">
            <h4>PubMed Grader <span class="s">2★</span></h4>
            <p>Append NIH iCite metrics to a set of PubMed IDs.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://fda-approvals.cancerdatasci.org">
            <h4>FDA Approvals <span class="s">2★</span></h4>
            <p>Robustly check whether a drug is FDA approved.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="https://store.cancerdatasci.org">
            <h4>Data store</h4>
            <p>Public datasets and derived files, served from R2.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="writing">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Writing</h2>
        <div class="note">Books, manuscripts, and methods.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="writing">
        <div class="wrow">
          <span class="wkind">Book</span>
          <div>
            <p class="wtitle"><a href="https://seandavi.github.io/RBiocBook/">Data Science for Biologists: A Hands-On Introduction with R and Bioconductor</a></p>
            <p>An instructional book grown from ~100 trainees across four course offerings.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wrow">
          <span class="wkind">Book</span>
          <div>
            <p class="wtitle"><a href="https://seandavi.github.io/amc-ai-governance/">Implementing AI at an Academic Medical Center</a></p>
            <p>A working book on AI governance and adoption in academic medicine.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wrow">
          <span class="wkind">Publications</span>
          <div>
            <p class="wtitle"><a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8991-6458">Full record on ORCID</a></p>
            <p>Peer-reviewed publications across genomics, informatics, and cancer data science.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="notes-slot">
        <a href="/blog">Notes</a> — release notes, build logs, and short technical pieces on the tools,
        data, and methods behind this work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="talks">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Talks &amp; teaching</h2>
        <div class="note">Recent lectures from the Frontiers of AI in Medicine course and invited talks.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="writing">
        {recentTalks.map((t) => (
          <div class="wrow">
            <span class="wkind">{t.dateLabel}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="wtitle"><a href={t.url}>{t.title}</a></p>
              <p>{t.description}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="notes-slot"><a href="/talks">All talks &amp; teaching</a> — a 2022–2025 archive, mostly AI/ML in medicine and data science.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cdsci" style="border-bottom: none;">
      <div class="band">
        <p>
          Much of the data-infrastructure work above lives under an open program,
          <strong style="font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)">Cancer Data Science</strong> — OmicIDX,
          CFDE Atlas, curated datasets, and more.
        </p>
        <a href="https://cancerdatasci.org">cancerdatasci.org</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="about" id="about">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>About</h2>
        <p>
          I'm a physician-scientist and Professor of Medicine at the University of Colorado Anschutz
          Medical Campus, where I'm Associate Director for Informatics and Data Science in the
          Comprehensive Cancer Center and Deputy Director of the Center for Health AI.
        </p>
        <p class="qual">
          I build open data infrastructure and AI tooling for cancer research, maintain long-standing
          software in the Bioconductor project, and help lead community open-science efforts. Reach me
          through any of the channels below.
        </p>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/seandavi">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.co.uk/citations?user=hLFc29kAAAAJ">Google Scholar</a>
          <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8991-6458">ORCID</a>
          <a href="/files/CV.pdf">CV</a>
          <a href="https://twitter.com/seandavis12">X / @seandavis12</a>
          <a href="mailto:seandavi@gmail.com">Email</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <footer>
      <div class="colophon">
        <strong style="color:var(--muted);font-weight:600">seandavis.net</strong> — open tools and data for
        cancer research, by Sean Davis. Data-infrastructure work lives at
        <a href="https://cancerdatasci.org">cancerdatasci.org</a>.
      </div>
      <div>© 2026 Sean Davis · Built in the open</div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Base>
